READ: CO2, the MIXED LAYER and the LAND tie at roundoff -- the test's own
claim SURVIVES the pump for total carbon. `ocean_C` differs by a CONSTANT
(the two circulations store different PREINDUSTRIAL interior inventories);
its TRANSIENT ties. What genuinely breaks is the ISOTOPES.
Both hemispheres break the SAME WAY: ml_C13 NH 9.19e-06, SH 1.14e-05 (ratio 1.24,
against the SH/NH ocean-area ratio 1.33) -- a scaling, not a swap.


=== PART 3 -- P2: what the transpose preserves, on the OPERATORS alone ===
t = 10 yr : (ml,ml) = 0.5866462195 both ways, |gap| 0.000e+00
            max_{k>1} |(ml,k)_up - (ml,k)_out| = 4.024e-01
t = 60 yr : (ml,ml) = 0.0407622203 both ways, |gap| 0.000e+00
            max_{k>1} |(ml,k)_up - (ml,k)_out| = 2.196e-01

P2 CONFIRMED. The mixed-layer DIAGONAL element is preserved EXACTLY (a
bit-identical 0, not a small number); the INTERIOR-to-mixed-layer elements
differ by O(1). A source at the mixed layer is invariant under the
reversal; a source in the interior is not. The pump is the model's FIRST
interior source, which is why the tie survived until it landed.


