P4 CONFIRMED: CO2 goes 8.53e-13 (N, fixed export MASS) -> 5.32e-02 (D, export
scaled by mixed-layer DIC), a factor of 6e+10.
So it is STATE-DEPENDENCE of the interior source, not its mere presence,
that reaches the atmosphere. Mode N fixes the export's MASS but NOT its
ISOTOPIC RATIO -- which tracks the mixed layer's own and moves with the
Suess effect -- so the isotopes break in mode N and 12C does not.


