moves inside the window, and CO2 stays at roundoff in EVERY window.
CAVEAT, stated rather than hidden: the 1750-1770 arm is not a zero-forcing
control -- it still carries a 0.44 permil start-up transient off the
spinup, so it BOUNDS the break from above rather than isolating zero.


=== VERDICT ===
test-ocean-advection.R's claim was ALWAYS CONDITIONAL on the ocean having
no interior source, and said so in its own words -- 'the mixed layer is the
ONLY box coupling the ocean to the rest of the model'. The pump falsifies
that premise, not the theorem. NOT A BUG:
  * CO2, the mixed layer and the land still tie EXACTLY (P3), at every
    pump_grad tested including 2x the shipped default;
  * `ocean_C`'s 1352 GtC gap is a preindustrial-inventory OFFSET, flat to
    1e-10 across the run, not a transient;
  * the isotope break is ~1e-3 permil in atmospheric d13C, against a
    likelihood sigma of 0.44 permil -- 0.4 % of one sigma.
The re-derived test should assert the CONDITIONAL claim plus its boundary,
which is STRONGER than what it asserts today: (a) 12C invariant with the
pump ON, (b) `ocean_C` a constant offset, (c) the isotopes MUST break, and
(d) a pump-OFF arm recovering the original all-columns tie.


